The Real Roadmap To AGI
This is the honest path. Not 5 versions. Years of work.

Stage 1 — Language Quality (Current)
You are here → V22

Remaining work:
  Coherent sentence generation
  Factual question answering
  Simple reasoning tasks

How to get there:
  Scale to 100M parameters
  Train on 1B+ tokens
  Add proper LM head

Estimated time: 3-6 months
Success metric: Perplexity < 50 on held-out text

Stage 2 — Grounded Understanding
Current AGNIS sees tokens.
AGI needs to understand what tokens mean.

What this requires:
  Multimodal input (text + images + audio)
  Symbol grounding — connecting words to concepts
  Embodied interaction — learning from environment

Key addition needed:
  Visual cortex module (process images)
  Connect "cat" token to cat image
  Build visual-linguistic associations

This is where AGNIS predictive coding
has a huge advantage — the brain does
exactly this through predictive vision

Stage 3 — Causal World Model
Current: AGNIS predicts "what comes next"
AGI needs: "what would happen if"

What this requires:
  Mental simulation capability
  Counterfactual reasoning
  "If I do X, then Y will happen"

Key addition:
  World model layer above language
  Can simulate hypothetical scenarios
  Builds causal graphs from experience

AGNIS predictive coding is actually
well-suited for this — prediction IS
causal modeling at a basic level

Stage 4 — Working Memory + Reasoning
Current: 16-256 token context window
AGI needs: Arbitrary reasoning chains

What this requires:
  Scratchpad memory for multi-step reasoning
  Ability to hold intermediate results
  Chain reasoning steps together

Key addition:
  Hippocampal fast-write memory (you have this)
  + Working memory buffer (new)
  + Reasoning controller (new)

This is where your hippocampal module
becomes critical — it was built for this

Stage 5 — Curiosity + Agency
Current: Passive — waits for input
AGI needs: Active — seeks information

What this requires:
  Intrinsic motivation system
  Curiosity-driven exploration
  Goal setting and pursuit
  Self-directed learning

Key addition:
  Free energy minimization as action selection
  "Which action reduces my uncertainty most?"
  Agent that reads documents to answer questions
  Agent that runs experiments to test hypotheses

You identified this gap in V5.0 analysis —
this is V10.0 on your original roadmap

Stage 6 — Self Improvement
AGI must improve its own learning algorithms

What this requires:
  Meta-learning — learning how to learn
  Architecture modification at runtime
  Evaluating own performance accurately
  Identifying own knowledge gaps

Key addition:
  Self-monitoring meta-controller
  Can modify its own hyperparameters
  Can grow new architectural components
  Based on performance assessment

AGNIS neurogenesis is the seed of this —
the network already grows new structure
The next step is growing BETTER structure
not just MORE structure

Stage 7 — General Intelligence
This is where AGI emerges from the combination:

Language quality          → Stage 1 ✓
Grounded understanding    → Stage 2
Causal world model        → Stage 3
Working memory + reasoning → Stage 4
Curiosity + agency        → Stage 5
Self improvement          → Stage 6
                               ↓
                    General Intelligence

No single addition creates AGI.
It emerges from all components working together.
